  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="13cd-cb01-1551-a972" name="Ligurian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #14 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Ligurian Tribes occupied an area of North-western Italy, controlling access to Gaul and living in both the mountain areas and various river valleys Including the Rhone and Po, they were fiercely independent warriors resisting all incursions but willing to supply mercenaries or ally with any power if they felt this to be sufficiently within their interests. As with Thrace and Illyria the tribes also fought amongst themselves and were unlikely to menace a non-aggressive neighbour unless temporarily united in a confederation. The Tribes supported Carthage during the Punic wars and afterward fought a long and bitter struggle against Rome, only being defeated with great difficulty in the late second century bc. even so it was not until the time of Augustus that the alpine tribes were finally subjugated. The list represents one of the most important tribes such as the Ingauni or Interemeli 

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Ligurian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Skirmishers: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Skirmishers: Up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
